{"id": 22, "ts": 1780459564.2572703, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I\u2019m less convinced that Candidate\u202fA remains the strongest option now that we have confirmed there\u2019s no concrete evidence of his stress\u2011resilience, crew\u2011cooperation or adaptability. Those are core safety\u2011critical criteria for long\u2011distance flights, and the \u201cshow\u2011off\u201d and \u201cnot open to new ideas\u201d notes only hint at possible issues without proving they\u2019re absent.\nIn contrast, Candidate\u202fC is documented as\u202f100\u202f% reliable and creates a positive crew atmosphere\u2014direct evidence of operational reliability and crew cooperation. He also makes correct decisions quickly and has excellent attention skills, covering decision quality and information accuracy. While his communication style and egocentric tendency are concerns, they are outweighed by the solid, safety\u2011relevant record we do have.\nGiven the current evidence gap for A and the concrete strengths of C, I now recommend **Candidate\u202fC** as the provisional lead, pending any further clarification on his adaptability or education willingness."}
